    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2ApjJf3fNB4nmVud6MqNpBi)_\n\n**Before:** `sp-vulpea-hierarchy` knew one relation, `parent`, read from one metadata key (`vulpea-hierarchy-parent-key`).\n\n**After:** `vulpea-hierarchy-relations` declares any number of relations. Each has a label, a colour and a list of sources: a metadata key (`- supports :: [[id:..][..]]`), the inverse of a metadata key (`- children ::` on a parent gives its children their parent edge), or a file property such as `DG_SUPPORTS` (and the inverse of a property). `parent` still builds the tree; `supports`, `opposes`, `informs` and `answers` are declared as defaults, the same names `discourse-graphs` uses. The other relations appear as dashed, labelled, coloured links between two notes that are both in view, in the browser page (with a legend) and in the SVG export. The outlines are unchanged. `vulpea-hierarchy-parent-key` is removed: its value is now the `parent` relation's `(meta \"parents\")` source.\n\n**How:** `vulpea-hierarchy--edges` reads every source into `(subject relation object)` edges and drops duplicates; `--build` turns `parent` edges into the tree and keeps the rest as `:links`; `--scope` keeps the links whose two ends are in scope. Tested on mock notes with a file property, an inverse key, a repeated key and a comma-separated key, plus a JavaScript syntax check, `dot`, and a headless Chromium screenshot. Property sources have to test every note, because vulpea has no property index. Not run against your real vault, and I did not check how vulpea fills `vulpea-note-properties` there, so please confirm `DG_SUPPORTS` links show up. The literate doc is regenerated and tangles back byte for byte.\n\nThe links are drawn between boxes without choosing where they sit; placing them by direction is the follow-up PR in this stack.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YKB9W9Svzsc4PYxBD8qL9Q)_",
